gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: What Owners Should Know</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Wisconsin</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession sale</li><li>Turn the Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Wisconsin House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Wisconsin law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Adverse possession not founded on a written instrument: 20 years of uninterrupted adverse possession bars an owner&#x27;s action for recovery of possession. (Wis. Stat. 893.25(1); <a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/893.25' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Possession is adverse under 893.25 only if the possessor is in actual continued occupation under claim of title, exclusive of any other right, and the land is protected by a substantial enclosure or usually cultivated or improved. (Wis. Stat. 893.25(2); <a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/893.25' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A 7-year period applies where the possessor meets the 10-year requirements and also pays all real estate taxes for the 7 years after original entry. (Wis. Stat. 893.27(1), (2)(b); <a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/893.27' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Landlord may hold personal property left by a trespasser removed from residential rental property for 7 days before disposing of it. (Wis. Stat. 704.055(2)(a); <a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/704.05' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Wisconsin?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Wisconsin houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Wisconsin house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Wisconsin attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wisconsin-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Wisconsin Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wisconsin-eviction-notice/'>Wisconsin Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wisconsin-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Wisconsin guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-wisconsin/'>We buy houses in Wisconsin</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/893.25' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Wis. Stat. 893.25(1)</a></li><li><a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/893.27' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Wis. Stat. 893.27(1), (2)(b)</a></li><li><a href='https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/statutes/704.05' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Wis. Stat. 704.055(2)(a)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Wisconsin house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Wisconsin attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Wisconsin\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-wisconsin/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wisconsin-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Wisconsin Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Wisconsin squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "wisconsin squatters rights"}, {"slug": "wisconsin-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Wisconsin Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1